.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-nodes-set - Set the extra node count


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container nodes set  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the extra node count

.PP
Adds or removes extra nodes of the plan's node size (absolute \fBextra_nodes\fR, 0 = plan only; at most 20 nodes per environment in total, GyroKota may lower it). An extra node costs the same as a plan node, billed hourly from the prepaid balance. Removing drains first: replicas move to the remaining nodes (services restart one by one, health checked), then the node is deleted; it is not billed while drained. Refused with 409 \fBquota_in_use\fR when the remaining nodes cannot hold the running services. Serverless environments have no nodes. Needs \fB"confirm": true\fR\&. Every change of a dedicated environment's node set (plan change, extra node added or removed) is announced BEFORE the old nodes go: as soon as the new nodes' addresses are known (usually under a minute) the owner is notified (Alerts channels, event \fBegress\fR) and \fBegress_change\fR / \fBpending_egress_ips\fR show them. With the approval step on (\fBPUT /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-approval\fR, 1-72 hours, 24 recommended) the new nodes take no traffic and the old nodes keep serving until \fBPOST /cloud/containers/{id}/egress-change/approve\fR or the deadline (then it continues by itself). A removal only never waits.

.PP
API: PUT /cloud/containers/{id}/nodes (operationId setContainerNodes, scope services_write)


